  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Updated to DuckDB v2.0.0\n\nBreaking changes:\n- DuckDB.NET.Bindings 2.0 needs DuckDB.NET.Data 2.0: DuckDB.NET.Data 1.x with Bindings 2.0 throws TypeLoadException at the first string append. Upgrade both packages together\n- DuckDBString.value and the nested type DuckDBString._value_e__Union are removed: read a string with Length and Data, and build a short one with DuckDBString.TryCreateInlined\n- DuckDBString.TryCreateInlined returns true for a short string that contains a NUL character; it returned false\n- NativeMethods.Value.DuckDBCreateVarchar takes a non-nullable string (null crashes the process; use DuckDBCreateNullValue for NULL), and has a new overload for UTF-8 bytes, DuckDBCreateVarchar(ReadOnlySpan<byte>), which keeps NUL characters. With C# 12, DuckDBCreateVarchar(null) and DuckDBCreateVarchar(default) are ambiguous, and a method group or a reflection lookup of DuckDBCreateVarchar needs the parameter type\n- DuckDBStringInlined is internal: build a short string with DuckDBString.TryCreateInlined\n- DuckDBValue.GetValue<T> gives the value as its own type, as object, a nullable of it or an interface it implements; any other T throws InvalidCastException. It reinterpreted the value's memory as T\n\nNew features:\n- DuckDBHugeInt and DuckDBUHugeInt can be created from an Int128 and a UInt128\n- DuckDBType has the DuckDB 1.5 types STRING_LITERAL, INTEGER_LITERAL, TIME_NS, GEOMETRY and VARIANT\n- Bindings for duckdb_prepared_statement_type, duckdb_clear_bindings and duckdb_create_varchar_length\n\nFixes:\n- Some native function declarations were corrected to match duckdb.h",
